{"title":"Internally tangent","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">geometry</a>, two <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Circle\" title=\"Circle\">circles</a> are considered to be internally tangent if they are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Tangent\" title=\"Tangent\">tangent</a> to each other and the center of one is inside the other. If the radii of two internally tangent circles is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae8889150ef5f04b9b7fdf6abc17e11410198ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r_1, r_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"11\" />, then the distance of their centers to each other is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/a/fbabfaa9ccb3f603dc4e7bce633e340e1e89dbcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|r_1 - r_2|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Internally_tangent&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018091547\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.012 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 13/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 295/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 359/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.503      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.503      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:19974:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018091547 and revision id 136701. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}